        "response": {
          "output": "Add the Cinnamon agent to your build and pick an exporter. It needs an Akka subscription and the commercial resolver credentials, which you shouldn't commit.\n\n**sbt setup**\n```scala\n// project/plugins.sbt\naddSbtPlugin(\"com.lightbend.cinnamon\" % \"sbt-cinnamon\" % \"2.22.x\")\n\n// build.sbt\nenablePlugins(Cinnamon)\nrun / cinnamon := true\ntest / cinnamon := true\nlibraryDependencies ++= Seq(\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkka,           // required\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonPrometheus,     // a backend is required, or nothing is exported\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaTyped,\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaCluster,\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaPersistence,\n  Cinnamon.library.cinnamonAkkaStream\n)\n```\nAdd only the toolkit modules you actually use. The skill gives the same setup for Maven and Gradle but not the details, so check the docs for those.\n\n**Opt in to actor metrics.** They're off by default, so add this in `application.conf`:\n```hocon\ncinnamon.akka.actors { \"/user/*\" { report-by = class } }\n```\nDon't instrument every actor, because that makes the metric count explode.\n\n**Running it.** The sbt plugin attaches the `-javaagent` for `run` and `test`. In production, attach the agent on every node. Each node reports independently.\n\n**Backends.** Prometheus, OpenTelemetry, Datadog and StatsD are supported. Jaeger and Zipkin cover tracing. Grafana dashboards are available.\n\nWhich build tool and backend are you using? I can give you the exact config."
